  "brief_description": "This young man with flowing hair is Philip the Handsome, son of the Holy Roman Emperor and founder of the Habsburg dynasty in Spain, so-called because of his fair hair and attractive grey eyes. The painting is one wing of a diptych (a panel painting in two parts). The other, showing his sister, Margaret of Austria, is also in the National Gallery's collection.\n\nPhilip wears the collar of the Order of the Golden Fleece, a prestigious chivalric order founded by Philip the Good, Duke of Burgundy, in the 1430s. The artist has minimised his prognathism -- an inherited condition where the lower jaw sticks out forwards, the so-called 'Habsburg jaw'.",
